      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Heribert Pohl --- Thanks for half  a million clicks! from Germering bei München, Bayern",
      "description": "Probably the castle was built around 1110 by brothers Adolf and Eberhard von Berg above the river Lenne on the Hill Wulfseck . The first name was Wulfhagen. Later it was renamed in Altena . 1392 the Earl  moved from the harsh Sauerland to his their new primary residence near Hamm. From then on the castle of Altena was only bailiff seat. Later the castle was the Prussian garrison and hospital. At the initiative of the district administrator Fritz Thomée the märkische castle club was founded in 1906.The club wanted to rebuild the castle The work was completed in 1918. 1914 Richard founded Schürmann within the walls of the castle the first youth hostel in the world. This rooms can still be seen today and are part of the Museum of the castle. Today, the city of  Altena ist owner of the castle. It houses multiply museums. According to legend, the name Altena is based on the low german term ‚al te na‘, what means ‚it is to near‘. The Counts castle of Arnsberg was too close to the new castle.",
